## Example of the required level
For a case whose subject is loopback interfaces:

<ul>
  <li>A loopback interface can be given an address, and can be reached at that address.</li>
  <li>A loopback address can be used as the source address for traffic the device sends.</li>
  <li>A loopback address can be advertised to other devices.</li>
  <li>More than one loopback interface can exist at the same time.</li>
  <li>An address that is not valid cannot be added to a loopback interface.</li>
  <li>Removing a loopback interface, or its address, really does remove it.</li>
</ul>

Note what the example does NOT contain: no list of address types or prefix lengths, no
timings, no product names, and nothing about features other than loopback interfaces.

Produce ONLY the HTML <ul> of bullets for the objective. No other text.
